     Upon successful completion, cclloossee__rraannggee() returns a value of 0.  Other‐
     wise, a value of -1 is returned and the global variable _e_r_r_n_o is set to
     indicate the error.

EERRRROORRSS
     The cclloossee__rraannggee() system call will fail if:

     [EINVAL]           The _h_i_g_h_f_d argument is lower than the _l_o_w_f_d argument.

     [EINVAL]           An invalid flag was set.

